docs {
  # GET /v1/usage-units/{id}

  Single UsageUnit with its nested MeasuringPoints. Each MeasuringPoint is
  the stable anchor across device replacements — use the
  `measuring_point_id` on drill-down calls, not the `device_id` (devices
  change, measuring points persist).

  ## Default `id`

  `280bb3c7-07db-4ef2-b0dc-9505096e676b` = **WE 01** (Musterstraße 2-4) — the
  unit with the meter-replacement scenario on `water_warm`.

  ## Units of Musterstraße 2-4

  | Name | Notable | id |
  |---|---|---|
  | WE 01 | `water_warm` replaced 2025-06-12 | `280bb3c7-07db-4ef2-b0dc-9505096e676b` |
  | WE 02 | `water_cold` with `calibration_expired` | `b47f82ea-7555-4b3e-a822-0dcd67e36197` |
  | WE 03 | `water_outdoor` (garden tap) | `38bd0ccc-5b88-4be0-bcef-3d4f4da8a13b` |
  | WE 04 | `hca` with K-factors 0.625 and 1.25 | `8b07a7de-f834-4cce-9f89-87ef6785b4b1` |
  | WE 05 | `hca` data gap | `fe4941e2-1036-418f-b0f0-4392e21916eb` |
  | WE 06 | `water_warm` difference meter | `42f9dc37-bee9-411e-96b4-86c5e5c395d9` |
  | WE 07 | reserved `electricity` / `gas` | `4be11437-c4a7-424a-8028-85edebe6a8ac` |
  | GE 01 | commercial unit | `4268fed0-4b16-4ebe-aaa4-94d129aed47c` |
}
